# Financial wrapper prospective cumulative accounting review

**Decision: the narrowly defined synthetic financial-wrapper program may legitimately have its own prospective family and finite 18-attempt allocation. Registration, actual allowance adoption and execution remain WITHHELD.** This is a substantive accounting interpretation of draft `060e13c4534747393591e30f60ba38fe105a9b8782260a0b75575cf3b7775564`; it is not an accepted-extension token, registry mutation, claim reservation or native release.

Independent metadata reconstruction passed 1,577 assertions across 11 explicitly bounded genuine ledger roots, including 88 recorded claim copies. No existing claim with the proposed program/mechanism or any of its 18 proposed identities was found there. The scope is enumerated in `HISTORY_READBACK01.json`; this does not establish universal or future namespace freshness. Exact claim/terminal/body hashes, current source-interface hashes and each ledger root are retained. One reader initially refused the genuine historical seven-day claim's two-link file; the original failed script and correction are preserved. Only that exact claim and its terminal received a two-link read exception. Their hashes match the original historical manifest; no exclusive-ownership claim follows.

The distinction rests on the actual question and implementation, not the new names. The wrapper tests original `fit_cell` 100-epoch execution, a genuine one-update interrupted FAILED parent, 99-update continuation, separate uninterrupted reference, and saved completed-model prediction on 448 distinct synthetic graphs per 16×28 batch. Its selected candidate requires graph checkpointing false (`financial_execution.py:87,109`). It is neither the old checkpoint-false/true two/28-graph proof, cold feature detachment/lifetime/joint-gradient acceptance, empirical dictionary import nor paper/full-graph capacity. Source reuse, original model20f451, seed11 and engineering knowledge remain related exposure and must be disclosed. A future claim of the old failed mechanism under this new name would invalidate the distinct-family interpretation and require cumulative same-mechanism review.

Actual history is preserved as follows:

| Account | Independently joined actual history | Accounting consequence |
|---|---|---|
| Paper | Original 17 identities and all historical metadata pins, plus 19 current program claims = 36 unique closed; 27 COMPLETE, 9 FAILED; maximum adopted current ceiling 64 | No paper65, refund, spare-quota transfer or financial-fit credit. |
